  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 142 AM CDT Sun May 31 2026\n\nModels continue to be in good overall agreement with low spread\namong the different models and their ensembles that initially,\nthe Omega Block pivots to become oriented from northwest to \nsoutheast with the ridging at the surface and aloft located \nacross the area Tuesday through Wednesday night. This will bring\na return to cool nights and warm days to the area through \nmidweek. As the high shifts to the east Wednesday into Thursday,\nthat will begin to draw Gulf moisture northward toward the \narea. \n\nWednesday into Thursday, models continue to show the Omega Block\nbreakdown and shift to the east as a shortwave and closed low \nmoves along the US Canadian border and suppresses the ridge. As\nthis feature passes to the north, it drives a cool front across\nthe area. Model consensus forecast continues to show 20 to 45 \npercent chances of showers and storms across the area Thursday \nafternoon through Saturday. Again, any rainfall amounts will be \nlight. Temperatures will slowly warm Wednesday through the end\nof the week.",
